// A lift in a 3.5 m shaft, balanced by hand. The cage (60 kg) with the mole on it (30 kg) is heavier than the
// bare counterweight (40 kg), so it sits at the foot. Six stones of ballast loaded from the cage (60 kg more)
// make the counterweight the heavier and it rises, carrying the mole to the top; the head's brake holds it
// to 2 m/s. Take the six stones back and the cage sinks to the foot again.
map
##############################
##############################
#########............#########
#########............#########
#########............#########
#########............#########
#########............#########
#########............#########
#########............#########
#########............#########
#########............#########
#########............#########
#########............#########
#########............#########
#########............#########
#########............#########
#########..@.........#########
##############################
##############################
end
give Lift 1
give Stone 10
place 2 4 -2 Lift                 // the head hangs under the shaft's ceiling; the cage starts at the foot
expect 3 lifts == 1
expect 3 lifty > 14
hold 5-20 right                   // step onto the cage (it spans the shaft's middle)
expect 60 liftv == 0              // cage and mole outweigh the bare counterweight
wield 61 Stone
use 62 4 -1
use 64 4 -1
use 66 4 -1
use 68 4 -1
use 70 4 -1
use 72 4 -1
expect 73 ballast == 6
expect 110 liftv < 0              // rising
expect 110 liftv > -9             // no faster than the brake allows (8 tiles/s)
expect 300 lifty < 5              // at the top of the shaft...
expect 300 py < 5                 // ...with the mole on it
expect 300 inv:Stone == 4
wield 301 none
use 302 4 -14
use 304 4 -14
use 306 4 -14
use 308 4 -14
use 310 4 -14
use 312 4 -14
expect 313 ballast == 0
expect 600 lifty > 14             // down at the foot again, mole and all
expect 600 py > 14
saveload 601                      // the lift and its ballast are saved
expect 602 lifts == 1
